1. What you may do

   You may download, open, use and change the SDK, inside the SDK, only to make, test and publish
   maps for the game Super Monster Tag, for example on its Steam Workshop.

   You may share the maps you make with it. A map package exported by the SDK names the SDK's files
   rather than containing them, and you may share such packages freely.

2. What you may not do

   You may not use the SDK, or any part of it, outside the SDK or for any other purpose. In
   particular, you may not:
   - use any of its files (code, models, textures, shaders or anything else), whole or in part, in
     another game, application, engine, mod or project, whether free or commercial;
   - copy its files out of the SDK to use them anywhere else;
   - sell, sublicense or redistribute the SDK or any part of it on its own, or include it in
     anything other than a Super Monster Tag map made with the SDK as described above.

3. Your own work

   The maps you make, and any models, textures and other files you create yourself and add to
